"Tap the photo to focus. A wider aperture blurs areas away from the focus plane." = "Tap the photo to focus. A wider aperture blurs areas away from the focus plane.";
"Depth is estimated on device once per photo or geometry change. Hair and transparent objects can have imperfect edges. Increasing the aperture number softens the effect." = "Depth is estimated on device once per photo or geometry change. Hair and transparent objects can have imperfect edges. Increasing the aperture number softens the effect.";
"Depth Lens model is missing." = "Depth Lens model is missing.";

/* Depth Lens detailed help */
"Depth of field and focus by touch" = "Depth of field and focus by touch";
"Depth Lens simulates depth of field from an estimated depth map. It can blur areas in front of and behind the selected focus plane. The original photo is preserved; the effect is off by default." = "Depth Lens simulates depth of field from an estimated depth map. It can blur areas in front of and behind the selected focus plane. The original photo is preserved; the effect is off by default.";
"Start with the focus" = "Start with the focus";
"Enable Depth Lens, then tap the subject in the photo while this tab is open. The turquoise marker shows the selected position. On a portrait, start with the nearest eye. This tap sets focus instead of opening the full-screen view." = "Enable Depth Lens, then tap the subject in the photo while this tab is open. The turquoise marker shows the selected position. On a portrait, start with the nearest eye. This tap sets focus instead of opening the full-screen view.";
"The focus plane" = "The focus plane";
"The effect uses the estimated distance at the selected point, not a cutout of the subject. Other objects at a similar estimated depth can remain sharp. A face or body spanning several depths may not be entirely sharp." = "The effect uses the estimated distance at the selected point, not a cutout of the subject. Other objects at a similar estimated depth can remain sharp. A face or body spanning several depths may not be entirely sharp.";
"Center focus returns the marker to the middle of the photo. It does not detect or select a face automatically." = "Center focus returns the marker to the middle of the photo. It does not detect or select a face automatically.";
"Shape the blur" = "Shape the blur";
"A small f-number, such as f/1.4, gives stronger blur and a narrower sharp region. A larger number, such as f/5.6 or f/8, reduces the blur. If an eye or hair becomes too soft, increase the number and check the focus position." = "A small f-number, such as f/1.4, gives stronger blur and a narrower sharp region. A larger number, such as f/5.6 or f/8, reduces the blur. If an eye or hair becomes too soft, increase the number and check the focus position.";
"50, 85, and 135 mm change the simulated optical blur. At the same aperture and focus, longer focal lengths generally strengthen the blur. They do not zoom, crop, or change the perspective of the photo." = "50, 85, and 135 mm change the simulated optical blur. At the same aperture and focus, longer focal lengths generally strengthen the blur. They do not zoom, crop, or change the perspective of the photo.";
"A restrained starting point" = "A restrained starting point";
"Try 50 or 85 mm with f/4, place the focus carefully, then lower the f-number gradually. Judge both the whole image and the edges around the subject. Strong blur makes depth-estimation errors more visible." = "Try 50 or 85 mm with f/4, place the focus carefully, then lower the f-number gradually. Judge both the whole image and the edges around the subject. Strong blur makes depth-estimation errors more visible.";
"Compare and correct" = "Compare and correct";
"Disable Depth Lens to compare with the same edits without this blur; enabling it again keeps its settings. Holding the photo compares with the original, before all edits. Pinch to inspect fine details and double-tap to restore the view." = "Disable Depth Lens to compare with the same edits without this blur; enabling it again keeps its settings. Holding the photo compares with the original, before all edits. Pinch to inspect fine details and double-tap to restore the view.";
"Reset turns the effect off and restores f/1.4, 85 mm, and centered focus. Undo and Redo include Depth Lens changes; the settings are saved with the photo." = "Reset turns the effect off and restores f/1.4, 85 mm, and centered focus. Undo and Redo include Depth Lens changes; the settings are saved with the photo.";
"Limits and rendering" = "Limits and rendering";
"Hair, glass, reflections, fine branches, and overlapping objects can produce imperfect depth boundaries. Inspect both eyes and the subject edges. Reduce the blur or disable the effect when the depth estimate is unsuitable; it does not reconstruct hidden background detail." = "Hair, glass, reflections, fine branches, and overlapping objects can produce imperfect depth boundaries. Inspect both eyes and the subject edges. Reduce the blur or disable the effect when the depth estimate is unsuitable; it does not reconstruct hidden background detail.";
"Depth is calculated on the iPhone and reused while adjusting aperture, focal length, or focus. The first activation may take longer. Changing crop, geometry, or optical corrections recalculates depth; check the focus again afterward." = "Depth is calculated on the iPhone and reused while adjusting aperture, focal length, or focus. The first activation may take longer. Changing crop, geometry, or optical corrections recalculates depth; check the focus again afterward.";
"The preview uses a reduced resolution while dragging, then a higher quality render when released. Export applies the same effect at the output resolution. The focus marker is never exported. Depth Lens affects the whole photo and cannot be assigned to a local mask." = "The preview uses a reduced resolution while dragging, then a higher quality render when released. Export applies the same effect at the output resolution. The focus marker is never exported. Depth Lens affects the whole photo and cannot be assigned to a local mask.";
"When Depth Lens is enabled and its tab is open, a short tap sets the focus point. Switch to another tab to use the usual full-screen tap." = "When Depth Lens is enabled and its tab is open, a short tap sets the focus point. Switch to another tab to use the usual full-screen tap.";
